<title>POLAND: Poland C/A deficit at $355 mln in March.</title>
<headline>Poland C/A deficit at $355 mln in March.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland had a current account deficit of $355 million in March bringing the shortfall in the first quarter to $1.487 billion, the National Bank of Poland said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>During the first quarter of 1996, Poland had a current account surplus of $151 million, the NBP said.  </p>
<p> POLISH CURRENT ACCOUNT	  MARCH 1997   FEBRUARY</p>
<p> current account million USD     -355	   -233</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	 -885	   -706</p>
<p> exports				1,920	  1,941</p>
<p> imports				2,805	  2,647</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	 423	    380</p>
<p>					 JAN-MARCH 1997   JAN-MARCH 1996</p>
<p> current account million USD    -1,487		  151</p>
<p> merchandise trade balance	-3,067	     -1,442</p>
<p> exports				 5,766		5,537</p>
<p> imports				 8,833		6,979</p>
<p> unclassified flows balance	1,216		1,820</p>
<p>Note: From January 1996 the central bank introduced a new category, &quot;unclassified flows&quot; which encompasses mainly cross-border, unregistered trade flows.</p>
<p>     -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
